"Amazon SageMaker AI":{"security":["Separate roles for data access, training, processing, model registry, endpoint invocation and monitoring; notebook users should not receive production deployment authority.","Use VPC-only networking where required, encrypt volumes, artifacts, endpoints and feature stores, and keep secrets out of notebooks and environment variables.","Audit jobs, lineage, models, endpoints and Studio changes; preserve approval and evaluation evidence for promoted models."],"optimization":["Choose processing, training, batch transform, real-time endpoints or serverless inference from latency and volume; do not keep an endpoint for an offline job.","Use instance types, autoscaling, multi-model endpoints, data formats and distributed training based on measured utilization and model size.","Separate experiment artifacts from production artifacts and use pipelines/registry gates to prevent accidental promotion."],"cost":["Amazon SageMaker AI cost follows its documented service unit: include request/query/message/byte, capacity, storage, or seat dimensions rather than using a generic compute estimate.","The dominant driver for Amazon SageMaker AI is workload-shaped: model volume, retention, retries, fan-out, idle capacity and cross-Region or cross-AZ transfer explicitly.","Include the adjacent services that Amazon SageMaker AI causes to run, such as S3, KMS, Lambda, logs, data transfer, indexes, endpoints or downstream databases."],"watchPoints":["SageMaker is a set of ML lifecycle components; a healthy endpoint does not prove model quality or data freshness.","Endpoint autoscaling, startup time, container image pull and model loading can dominate latency.","Training data, model artifact, feature values and inference code must be versioned together to reproduce a result."]},
